    "sha": "fe7403bca2fcb78e5a21c3f35c1cca32691af555",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGZlNzQwM2JjYTJmY2I3OGU1YTIxYzNmMzVjMWNjYTMyNjkxYWY1NTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:37:33Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:37:33Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim,app): read a containment kind's declared rim at the plain gouge tolerance on a reduced-fidelity model\n\nA Z drill, bore or thread mill verifies against rim loops that are our\nown 48+-gons of each hole's declared circle, built to half the gouge\ntolerance (0.0043 mm sag at a 2 mm radius). #864 tightened law (b) on\nevery loop by the model's excess, so past ~0.0057 mm of excess (a model\nflagged above ~0.0107 mm) a matched drill was convicted against its own\nrim at its first plunge, and a matched bore on its rings.\n\nVerifyContext now carries the declared rims; law (b) reads a loop that\ntraces one at the plain tolerance (today's full-fidelity verdict on it)\nand every other loop tightened. The solid law against the model's\nfacets is untouched, so an oversize, offset or past-the-floor drill\nstill convicts on the same coarse model.\n\nFixes #1057\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
